[Event "English vs 1...e5 (Reversed Sicilian)"]

{The English (1.c4) is a Sicilian with an extra tempo. White fights for d5 from the flank and fianchettoes on g2.}
1. c4 {[%csl Gd5] The English: controls d5 from the side. The pawn on c4 controls d5.}
1... e5 {The Reversed Sicilian. The pawn on e5 controls d4.}
2. Nc3 {Develops toward d5. The knight on c3 controls d5 and e4.}
2... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
 (2... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 controls d4.}
3. g3 {Fianchetto.}
3... g6 {Symmetrical.}
4. Bg2 {[%cal Gg2b7] The bishop rakes the long diagonal. The bishop on g2 eyes the knight on c6 and controls d5 and e4.}
4... Bg7 {Same idea.}
5. d3 {Flexible. The pawn on d3 controls e4.}
5... d6 {Solid.}
6. e4 {[%csl Gd5] The Botvinnik setup: a clamp on d5. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
)
3. Nf3 {Develops with pressure on e5. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on e5 and controls d4.}
3... Nc6 {Defends e5. The knight on c6 controls d4.}
4. g3 {Fianchetto.}
4... d5 {Black plays an Open Sicilian a tempo down.}
 (4... Bb4 {Pins the knight. The bishop on b4 eyes the knight on c3.}
5. Bg2 {Long diagonal.}
5... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... e4 {Gains space, kicking the knight. The pawn on e4 eyes the knight on f3.}
7. Ne1 {The knight re-routes to c2, and d3 will challenge e4.}
)
5. cxd5 {Takes. The pawn on d5 eyes the knight on c6.}
5... Nxd5 {Recaptures. The knight on d5 eyes the knight on c3.}
6. Bg2 {[%cal Gg2d5] Attacks the knight.}
6... Nb6 {Retreats. The knight on b6 controls d5.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... Be7 {Develops.}
8. d3 {Solid; prepares Be3 and a queenside expansion with a3 and b4.} *

[Event "English vs 1...c5 & 1...Nf6"]

{The Symmetrical English and the Anglo-Indian lines.}
1. c4 {The English. The pawn on c4 controls d5.}
1... c5 {The Symmetrical. The pawn on c5 controls d4.}
 (1... Nf6 {The Anglo-Indian. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
2. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5 and e4.}
2... e6 {Prepares ...d5. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
3. e4 {The Mikenas Attack. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
3... d5 {Counters. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c4 and the pawn on e4.}
4. e5 {[%cal Ge5f6] Kicks the knight. The pawn on e5 eyes the knight on f6.}
4... d4 {Black hits the c3-knight. The pawn on d4 eyes the knight on c3.}
5. exf6 {Takes the knight. The pawn on f6 eyes the pawn on g7.}
5... dxc3 {Takes back. The pawn on c3 eyes the pawn on b2 and the pawn on d2.}
6. bxc3 {Recaptures toward the centre. The pawn on c3 controls d4.}
6... Qxf6 {Regains the pawn. The queen on f6 eyes the pawn on c3 and the pawn on f2 and controls d4 and e5.}
7. d4 {[%csl Gd4] A strong centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
)
2. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
2... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
3. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5 and e4.}
3... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 controls d4 and e5.}
4. g3 {Fianchetto.}
4... d5 {Breaks in the centre. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls e4.}
5. cxd5 {Takes. The pawn on d5 eyes the knight on c6.}
5... Nxd5 {Recaptures. The knight on d5 eyes the knight on c3.}
6. Bg2 {[%cal Gg2d5] Hits the knight.}
6... Nc7 {Retreats, keeping d5 covered. The knight on c7 controls d5.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... e5 {The Rubinstein setup: a big centre. The pawn on e5 controls d4.} *
